                <pb facs="0233" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg167"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3731/961: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-20T16:00:00-05:00">August 20, 1934—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>424. For Welles: Turkel left today by plane with schedules I and II. Solano
                    apparently will be needed here until last minute. He says that he will arrive
                    Friday morning at 1 and will be prepared to go to work at once.</p>
                <p>Torriente will be accompanied also by Gabriel de la Campa, formerly Consul
                    General at Montreal, and Rodriguez Capote of the Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
